    "created_at": "2022-05-06T20:05:20Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-05-06T20:05:20Z",
    "body": "As I argue in <https://www.xanthir.com/b4wJ1>, strings shouldn't be iterable by default. Not all of the arguments there apply to Infra, but the second one (no right way to iterate a string) absolutely does.\r\n\r\nI think it would be fine to define `For each code point` and `For each code unit` that works over strings, tho.",
